>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `depth_limit`

``` hol4
tableauLib.depth_limit : int ref
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Controls the largest tableau resource bound tried by `BLAST_TAC`.

The initial value is 20. `BLAST_TAC` reads the reference when the tactic is
applied and, after preprocessing, searches bounds from 0 through the
current value. A negative value makes `BLAST_TAC` fail outright without
invoking the tableau engine. Use 0 for the minimal single-depth run.
`BLAST_DEPTH_TAC` and `tryIt` use their explicit arguments and do not
consult this reference.

The bound is not a timeout or literal formula depth. There is no automatic
time limit.

### Failure

Assigning the reference cannot fail. A value too small for a goal can make
`BLAST_TAC` fail to find a tableau proof.

### Example

``` hol4
val old_limit = !tableauLib.depth_limit;
val _ = tableauLib.depth_limit := 12;
```

Clients that change this global reference should normally restore it.

### See also

[`tableauLib.BLAST_TAC`](#tableauLib.BLAST_TAC),
[`tableauLib.BLAST_DEPTH_TAC`](#tableauLib.BLAST_DEPTH_TAC),
[`tableauLib.tryIt`](#tableauLib.tryIt)
